Subject: CBCharacteristic.service and CBService.peripheral are optional now

Apple made these weak optionals in iOS 15 / macOS 12 (2021). The vendored
snapshot is from 2022-02-18 but was built against an older SDK, so this one
line no longer compiles: under Swift 6.2 / the macOS 26 SDK it is

  error: value of optional type 'CBService?' must be unwrapped to refer to
         member 'peripheral' of wrapped base type 'CBService'

It is the ONLY line in the whole vendored set that fails. Verified by building
Session, BLESession, GATTHelpers, JSONRPCError, EncodingHelpers, RSSI,
DispatchSemaphore and both CoreBluetooth delegate helpers against Swift 6.2:
with this one change, "Build complete".

Optional-chaining is the minimal correct fix and matches what the API now
means — a characteristic whose service has been released has nothing to notify.

--- a/Sources/BLESession.swift
+++ b/Sources/BLESession.swift
@@
-            endpoint.service.peripheral.setNotifyValue(false, for: endpoint)
+            endpoint.service?.peripheral?.setNotifyValue(false, for: endpoint)
